  "worked_solution": "The matrix $P$ is singular if and only if $det(P)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =n\\cdot n-(-16)\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & ={n}^{2}-64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}^{2}-64 & =0 \\\\ {n}^{2} & =64 \\\\ n & =\\pm 8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the values of $n$ are $n=\\pm 8.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
